Z||000000||vinnywolfe||07-26-2000||10:59 PM||||went to a junkyard today for just a few trim pieces and such to finish up my 87gt.  they had been advertising a all you can carry for $35.  the place is going out of business.  anyway,  i didn't want to pay $35 for just a few pieces of trim (that didn't come out right).  that was the only way he said he'd let me in.  he told me he had a BUNCH of fieros.  paid the $35 and went in to have a look.  he has about 10-15 fieros (alot in one spot for around here).  most of them had a lot of salvagable stuff.  no engines.  but i'm going back saturday to "clean up".  if anyone has something in particular i can do my best to get it. <BR>for $35 i got:<BR>both power mirors and harnesses (there were more on other cars)<BR>variety of the speakers ( the ones on the pillar, not the 4x10's)<BR>both power lock actuators.<BR>half dozen or so power lock swithces.<BR>a couple oil press. swithces (v6 but there were alot of 4 banger stuff)<BR>visors (w/mirrors)<BR>power windows (motors and glass)<BR>spare tires<BR>NICE radio (the real nice ones they put in in later years)<BR>of course, my trim pieces<BR>headlamp and dimmer switches<P>i know there's more, i just can't remember it all.<P>anyone want me to look for anything in particular, i can't guarantee it, but i'll look.<BR>there were quite a few quarter windows (no cracks) for notchbacks.  also i saw a few notchbacks with what looked to be good tail lamp assemblys.<P>i just figured some of the parts off of these cars could be recycled before the cars were crunched.<P>let me know,<BR>vinny<BR> <BR> ||||reg||5
